Adversarial attacks on AI 
    Input image of a hummingbird and AI correctly labels it
        But we make a minor pertubation (slight change in pixels that is usually not                 noticable to humans)
        AI labels the images as a hammer, when it is still a hummingbird

Physical Attacks
    Ex. A man wearing a weird pair of glasses and AI thinks he is Milla Jovovich
    Ex. fooling an AI system into not seeing a stop sign by putting stickers on the sign

Adversarial defenses
    Defenses do exist, but incur some cost
    Similar t spam vs. anti-spam, we may be in an arms race for some applications
    
